WEBVTT

1
00:00:03.911 --> 00:00:17.135
Sign in and open Sales, then Quotations. Every offer you have made is listed here by status.

2
00:00:17.235 --> 00:00:20.303
Select New quotation to prepare an offer.

3
00:00:20.403 --> 00:00:26.430
Search for an existing customer by name or phone, and select them. Their pricing group applies.

4
00:00:26.530 --> 00:00:32.777
The issue date and the Valid until date are filled in. The offer is open for seven days by default.

5
00:00:32.877 --> 00:00:38.187
Search for products by name or SKU in the Items box and select each one to add it.

6
00:00:38.288 --> 00:00:43.489
Add as many products as the offer needs. Prices and taxes are filled in for you.

7
00:00:43.589 --> 00:00:46.865
Change a quantity and the line total updates.

8
00:00:46.965 --> 00:00:53.327
Check the summary at the bottom, then select Save draft.

9
00:00:53.427 --> 00:00:59.515
The quotation has its own number and starts as a Draft. Print gives you a copy for the customer.

10
00:00:59.616 --> 00:01:05.147
Select Mark as sent once you have given it to the customer. It does not send an email.

11
00:01:05.247 --> 00:01:08.951
When the customer agrees, select Accept.

12
00:01:10.252 --> 00:01:16.112
An accepted quotation can be converted. Select Convert to sale. This needs an open register.

13
00:01:16.212 --> 00:01:21.248
The items land in a sale at the POS, priced as quoted, ready to take payment.

14
00:01:21.348 --> 00:01:24.733
That is the quotation from first offer to sale.
